{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_014Rqvia74nGAksfRhRzJrRr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MVpkvfkEsURaBz4CMbNfzg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/coverage-auditor/output/gap-report.md","content":"# Test Coverage Gap Report\n\n**Library:** PathFinding.js  \n**Test suite:** `npx mocha --require should test/**/*.js`  \n**Result:** 57 passing, 0 failing  \n**Date:** 2026-04-16\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nAll finders pass 4 scenario-based maze tests each. Core utilities have basic happy-path tests. No edge-case, no-path, constructor option, or diagonal-variant coverage exists for most finders. Two finders are entirely untested. One utility function (`smoothenPath`) is completely absent from tests.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Node.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Implicitly exercised by every finder test (nodes created via Grid).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Direct construction: `new Node(x, y)` — default `walkable=true` branch\n- Explicit `walkable=false` constructor arg\n- No unit tests for Node in isolation\n\n**Priority:** Low — trivial constructor, but a dedicated unit test would catch regressions.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/DiagonalMovement.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Values referenced indirectly by Grid/finder tests.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- No test verifies the enum values (`Always=1`, `Never=2`, `IfAtMostOneObstacle=3`, `OnlyWhenNoObstacles=4`) are stable/correct\n- Invalid value passed to `Grid.getNeighbors` → should throw `'Incorrect value of diagonalMovement'` (branch at Grid.js:195) — **untested**\n\n**Priority:** Medium — the error-throw branch in `Grid.getNeighbors` is a real code path that is never exercised.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Grid.js\n\n**What IS tested:**\n- Constructor with `(width, height)` — no matrix\n- Constructor with `(matrix)` — no width/height\n- Constructor with `(width, height, matrix)`\n- `isWalkableAt`, `setWalkableAt`, `isInside`\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Never` and `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle`\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Always` — `d0=d1=d2=d3=true` branch (Grid.js:189)\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` — `d = s3 && s0` branch (Grid.js:180)\n- `getNeighbors` with invalid `diagonalMovement` → should `throw new Error('Incorrect value of diagonalMovement')` (Grid.js:195)\n- `_buildNodes` with mismatched matrix dimensions → should throw `'Matrix size does not fit'` (Grid.js:66)\n- `clone()` — never called in any test; cloned walkability not verified\n- `getNodeAt` — not tested directly (used internally only)\n- Corner node neighbor pruning (nodes at grid edges where diagonal would be out-of-bounds)\n\n**Priority:** High — `clone()` is used by finders internally but untested directly; matrix-mismatch and invalid diagonal-movement errors are completely uncovered.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Heuristic.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Nothing directly. Functions used implicitly by finders.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `manhattan(dx, dy)` — e.g. `manhattan(3, 4)` should return `7`\n- `euclidean(dx, dy)` — e.g. `euclidean(3, 4)` should return `5`\n- `octile(dx, dy)` — both `dx < dy` and `dx >= dy` branches\n- `chebyshev(dx, dy)` — e.g. `chebyshev(3, 4)` should return `4`\n- Zero inputs: all four functions with `(0, 0)` → should return `0`\n- Symmetry: `heuristic(a, b) === heuristic(b, a)` for octile/chebyshev\n\n**Priority:** High — pure functions, trivial to unit test, but zero coverage. Bugs here silently corrupt all heuristic-based finders.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Util.js\n\n**What IS tested:**\n- `interpolate(0, 1, 0, 4)` — vertical line only\n- `expandPath([])` — empty input\n- `expandPath([[0,1],[0,4]])` — two-segment path\n- `expandPath([[0,1],[0,4],[2,6]])` — three-segment path\n- `compressPath([])` — empty path (< 3 nodes, returns as-is)\n- `compressPath` — straight vertical then diagonal\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `interpolate` — horizontal line (`x0 != x1, y0 == y1`)\n- `interpolate` — diagonal line\n- `interpolate` — same start/end point (`x0==x1, y0==y1`) → single-element result\n- `backtrace` — no direct test; only exercised indirectly\n- `biBacktrace` — no direct test\n- `pathLength` — entirely untested; zero coverage\n- `smoothenPath` — entirely untested; the function also contains a **bug**: `lastValidCoord` is used without declaration (implicit global) at Util.js:167\n- `compressPath` with single-element path (length = 1) — boundary: returns path as-is\n- `compressPath` with two-element path (length = 2) — boundary\n\n**Priority:** High — `smoothenPath` has zero coverage AND contains an undeclared variable bug (`lastValidCoord` at line 167). `pathLength` and `biBacktrace` are completely untested.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/AStarFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios with default constructor (`DiagonalMovement.Never`, `manhattan` heuristic).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` + `octile`\n- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true, dontCrossCorners: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles`\n- Constructor with explicit `diagonalMovement` option (all four values)\n- Constructor with custom `heuristic` function\n- Constructor with `weight` != 1 (weighted A*)\n- No-path scenario (start/end isolated by walls) → should return `[]`\n- Start == End (same node) → should return `[[x,y]]` or `[]` — behavior unspecified/untested\n- `findPath` — neighbor already in open list with better g-score (the `openList.updateItem` branch at AStarFinder.js:116)\n\n**Priority:** High — the `weight`, custom heuristic, and no-path scenarios are critical behavioral paths with zero coverage.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/DijkstraFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (inherits AStarFinder with `heuristic = 0`).\n\n**What is NOT tested:** Same gaps as AStarFinder. Additionally:\n- Verify heuristic override to `0` — distances should reflect true uniform cost\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BestFirstFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal check only: start/end coords).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Custom heuristic injection\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- Constructor option coverage (same as AStarFinder)\n- The `* 1000000` scaling effect: on an open grid, path should be greedy (go straight to goal)\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BreadthFirstFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios with default options.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Diagonal movement enabled variants\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- Start == End\n- Constructor `allowDiagonal` / `dontCrossCorners` / `diagonalMovement` options\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BiAStarFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal check only).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- All constructor options (same as AStarFinder)\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- The `biBacktrace(node, neighbor)` meeting-point path join — only implicitly hit\n- The `biBacktrace(neighbor, node)` reverse direction join (end-side expansion finds start-side node)\n- Both expansion directions (start-side and end-side) meeting\n\n**Priority:** High — bi-directional meeting logic is complex and the two `biBacktrace` call sites are never explicitly asserted.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BiBreadthFirstFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (optimal check).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- Diagonal movement variants\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- `biBacktrace` call from end-side expansion (BiBreadthFirstFinder.js:100)\n- Start == End\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BiDijkstraFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (optimal).\n\n**What is NOT tested:** Same gaps as BiAStarFinder + DijkstraFinder.\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/BiBestFirstFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal).\n\n**What is NOT tested:** Same gaps as BestFirstFinder + bi-directional meeting logic.\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/IDAStarFinder.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal check only).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `trackRecursion: true` — `retainCount` and `tested` tracking branches (IDAStarFinder.js:137-144)\n- `timeLimit` option — path not found due to time expiry → `[]` (IDAStarFinder.js:105-108)\n- `weight` != 1\n- Custom heuristic\n- Diagonal movement variants\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- The `route` array construction (IDAStarFinder.js:118-121) — only implicitly verified\n\n**Priority:** High — `timeLimit` and `trackRecursion` are unique features with zero test coverage.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JumpPointFinder.js (factory)\n\n**What IS tested:**\n- `DiagonalMovement.Never` → `JPFNeverMoveDiagonally`\n- `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` → `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle`\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `DiagonalMovement.Always` → `JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally` — **no tests at all**\n- `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` → `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles` — **no tests at all**\n- Default (no option) → falls through to `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle`\n\n**Priority:** High — two of four factory branches (`Always`, `OnlyWhenNoObstacles`) produce untested finders.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Nothing — zero test coverage.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_jump` — diagonal movement detection of forced neighbors (JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally.js:43-51)\n- `_jump` — horizontal forced neighbor detection (line 56-59)\n- `_jump` — vertical forced neighbor detection (line 61-64)\n- `_jump` — end-node detection\n- `_jump` — out-of-bounds / unwalkable returns null\n- `_findNeighbors` — diagonal parent direction (line 94-110)\n- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent direction\n- `_findNeighbors` — vertical parent direction\n- `_findNeighbors` — no parent (returns all neighbors)\n- End-to-end `findPath` — any maze at all\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n\n**Priority:** High — entire file untested.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Nothing — zero test coverage.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_jump` — commented-out forced-neighbor check at line 44-47 (deliberate omission, but untested)\n- `_jump` — diagonal sub-jump calls (line 49)\n- `_jump` — horizontal forced neighbors (line 56-59)\n- `_jump` — vertical forced neighbors (line 62-65)\n- `_jump` — diagonal continuation gating (`isWalkableAt(x+dx,y) && isWalkableAt(x,y+dy)`) at line 75\n- `_findNeighbors` — all parent-direction branches\n- End-to-end `findPath` — any maze\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n\n**Priority:** High — entire file untested.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JPFNeverMoveDiagonally.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_jump` — horizontal direction forced-neighbor detection (line 42-45)\n- `_jump` — vertical direction + recursive horizontal sub-jumps (line 53)\n- `_jump` — `throw new Error(\"Only horizontal and vertical movements are allowed\")` (line 58) — diagonal dx/dy input never tested\n- `_jump` — `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent direction\n- `_findNeighbors` — vertical parent direction\n- `_findNeighbors` — no parent\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n\n**Priority:** High — error-throw branch and recursion path in `_jump` uncovered.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle.js\n\n**What IS tested:** 4 maze scenarios (non-optimal).\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_jump` — diagonal forced-neighbor detection branches (line 43-47)\n- `_jump` — diagonal continuation gating (`isWalkableAt(x+dx,y) || isWalkableAt(x,y+dy)`) at line 71 — the `null` return branch when both blocked\n- `_jump` — `trackJumpRecursion: true`\n- `_findNeighbors` — diagonal parent: forced neighbor additions at lines 110-115\n- `_findNeighbors` — horizontal parent: forced-obstacle-adjacent diagonal neighbors\n- `_findNeighbors` — no parent\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n\n**Priority:** High — diagonal continuation null-return branch and forced-neighbor pruning logic untested.\n\n---\n\n## src/finders/JumpPointFinderBase.js\n\n**What IS tested:** `findPath` loop runs via all JPF subclass tests.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `_identifySuccessors` — `jumpNode.closed` skip branch (line 89)\n- `_identifySuccessors` — `openList.updateItem` branch (ng < jumpNode.g, line 107)\n- `trackJumpRecursion: true` option (base class stores flag but never tested at base level)\n- No-path scenario (open list exhausted) → `[]`\n\n**Priority:** Medium.\n\n---\n\n## Cross-cutting gaps\n\n| Gap | Affected finders | Priority |\n|-----|-----------------|----------|\n| No-path (isolated start or end) returns `[]` | All 11 finders | **High** |\n| Start == End returns path | All finders | Medium |\n| `DiagonalMovement.Always` end-to-end | JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally | **High** |\n| `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` end-to-end | JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles | **High** |\n| `smoothenPath` — zero coverage + bug (undeclared `lastValidCoord`) | Util.js:167 | **High** |\n| `pathLength` — zero coverage | Util.js | **High** |\n| Heuristic unit tests | Heuristic.js | **High** |\n| `Grid.clone()` — zero direct coverage | Grid.js | High |\n| Matrix dimension mismatch error | Grid.js | Medium |\n| `IDAStarFinder` timeLimit expiry | IDAStarFinder.js | High |\n| `IDAStarFinder` trackRecursion | IDAStarFinder.js | Medium |\n| Deprecated `allowDiagonal` / `dontCrossCorners` options | AStarFinder, BFS, Dijkstra, … | Low |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":184,"cache_read_input_tokens":51895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":184},"output_tokens":72,"se