he error-throw branch in `Grid.getNeighbors` is a real code path that is never exercised.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Grid.js\n\n**What IS tested:**\n- Constructor with `(width, height)` — no matrix\n- Constructor with `(matrix)` — no width/height\n- Constructor with `(width, height, matrix)`\n- `isWalkableAt`, `setWalkableAt`, `isInside`\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Never` and `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle`\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Always` — `d0=d1=d2=d3=true` branch (Grid.js:189)\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` — `d = s3 && s0` branch (Grid.js:180)\n- `getNeighbors` with invalid `diagonalMovement` → should `throw new Error('Incorrect value of diagonalMovement')` (Grid.js:195)\n- `_buildNodes` with mismatched matrix dimensions → should throw `'Matrix size does not fit'` (Grid.js:66)\n- `clone()` — never called in any test; cloned walkability not verified\n- `getNodeAt` — not tested directly (used internally only)\n- Corner node neighbor pruning (nodes at grid edges where diagonal would be out-of-bounds)\n\n**Priority:** High — `clone()` is used by finders internally but untested directly; matrix-mismatch and invalid diagonal-movement errors are completely uncovered.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Heuristic.js\n\n**What IS tested:** Nothing directly. Functions used implicitly by finders.\n\n**What is NOT tested:**\n- `manhattan(dx, dy)` — e.g. `manhattan(3, 4)` should return `7`\n- `euclidean(dx, dy)` — e.g. `euclidean(3, 4)` should return `5`\n- `octile(dx, dy)` — both `dx < dy` and `dx >= dy` branches\n- `chebyshev(dx, dy)` — e.g. `chebyshev(3, 4)` should return `4`\n- Zero inputs: all four functions with `(0, 0)` → should return `0`\n- Symmetry: `heuristic(a, b) === heuristic(b, a)` for octile/chebyshev\n\n**Priority:** High — pure functions, trivial to unit test, but zero coverage. Bugs here silently corrupt all heuristic-based finders.\n\n---\n\n## src/core/Util.js\n\n**What IS tested